---
import site from '../data/site.json';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/posts';
---
<Base title="About" active="about">
  <section class="page-heading narrow"><h1>About the journal</h1></section>
  <article class="prose narrow stand-alone">
    <p class="lead">{site.title} is a weekly digest of psychology research.</p>
    <p>The English edition brings together selected psychology research in clear, readable language. It is a companion to a Chinese-language weekly digest, with its own space for articles and references.</p>
    <h2>What you’ll find here</h2><p>Weekly digests introduce a selection of papers, one study at a time. Research notes make room for a closer look at a particular question. Topics may range from relationships and learning to mental health and everyday decisions.</p>
    <h2>How the research is presented</h2><p>Every summary aims to explain who was studied, what the researchers did, and what they found. Limits and uncertainty belong in that explanation. An association is described as an association; a finding from one sample is kept in its context.</p>
    <p>References point back to the original papers. Publication dates distinguish online release from a later journal issue. Where a summary relies on an abstract, that basis is made clear.</p>
    <h2>Read along</h2><p>The English research archive is just beginning. You can browse the <a href={href('archive/')}>latest writing</a> or <a href={href('subscribe/')}>follow the RSS feed</a> for new posts.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
